    "body": "## Motivation\n\n`python/sglang/kernels/aot/setup_rocm.py` reads `AMDGPU_TARGET`, but then overwrites it with the arch of GPU 0 whenever `torch.cuda.is_available()`:\n\n```python\namdgpu_target = os.environ.get(\"AMDGPU_TARGET\", default_target)\nif torch.cuda.is_available():\n    amdgpu_target = torch.cuda.get_device_properties(0).gcnArchName.split(\":\")[0]\n```\n\nSo on any machine with a GPU, an explicit target is ignored without a warning. Building for gfx942 on an MI355X host produces a gfx950-only kernel, exits 0, and the wheel installs and imports cleanly. The mismatch only shows up on the target GPU.\n\nGPU-less builders, such as the Docker builds that pass `AMDGPU_TARGET=$GPU_ARCH_LIST`, never hit this because they take the `else` branch. The developer building on a workstation does hit it. The same fix is already on `amd_march` as part of #44308; this PR is just that behaviour, kept minimal for `main`.\n\n## Modifications\n\n- Autodetect only when `AMDGPU_TARGET` is unset or empty.\n- When it is set, use it and print that it came from the environment.\n- If detection fails, fall back to the default target as before, and say so in the warning.\n\nNothing changes when `AMDGPU_TARGET` is unset. That covers the AMD CI kernel build (`amd_ci_install_dependency.sh` runs `python3 setup_rocm.py install` without it), so CI behaviour is unchanged.\n\n## Accuracy Tests\n\nThis is build-only; no kernel or model code changed. Each row is one `setup_rocm.py build_ext --inplace` in `rocm/pytorch:rocm7.2.3_ubuntu24.04_py3.12_pytorch_release_2.10.0` on an MI355X host. The arch is read back from the built `common_ops*.so` with `llvm-objdump --offloading` (run on a copy, since it extracts the bundles next to its input).\n\n| source | `AMDGPU_TARGET` | GPU visible | offload bundles in `common_ops.so` |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| main | `gfx942` | gfx950 | **gfx950** (requested target ignored) |\n| this PR | `gfx942` | gfx950 | gfx942 |\n| main | unset | gfx950 | gfx950 |\n| this PR | unset | gfx950 | gfx950 (unchanged) |\n| this PR | unset | none | gfx942 (default, unchanged) |\n| this PR | `gfx950` | none | gfx950 (unchanged) |\n\n## Speed Tests and Profiling\n\nN/A (build script only).\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [x] Format your code according to the [Format code with pre-commit](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#format-code-with-pre-commit).\n- [ ] Add unit tests according to the [Run and add unit tests](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#run-and-add-unit-tests). (Not added: `setup_rocm.py` runs `setup()` at import, so a unit test would need to restructure the script. The table above is the verification.)\n- [x] Update documentation according to [Write documentations](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#write-documentations). (No doc change needed.)\n- [x] Provide accuracy and speed benchmark results. (N/A, build-only.)\n- [x] Follow the SGLang code style [guidance](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#code-style-guidance).\n\nPart of the plan in #46900 (Track A).\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:x: [Run #40610344518](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/40610344518)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #40610344489](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/40610344489)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:x: [Run #40610344519](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/40610344519)<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n<!-- pr-states:end -->",
